      "writtenOn": "2021-06-14T23:12:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. \nthere are two cases.\n1 - this command is run before USBC plugged in. then mfignore comes into picture from the start.\n\n2 - dock is already plugged in and assignment D was accepted. which means USB enumeration was USB3 and DP Aux 2-lane was negotiated.\n\nnow mfignore was run. But in this case, typeC need to be unplugged to initiate new 4-lane Aux negotiation. \nsame thing happens when we are in assignment C want to go back to Assignment D. USB need to reenumerated to USB3.\n\nMy understanding is initiating DP Aux negotiation and USB renumeration from EC context is not there now.",
      "parentUuid": "c1fa8e95_5d46e9c4",
      "revId": "054a7bf52e910d35afb6735331bd457f471fe255",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
